<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Great Pyramid of Giza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 2560 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/26th-century-bce">26th century BCE</a> · Also known as Pyramid of Khufu</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Great Pyramid of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/giza">Giza</a> was built for the Fourth Dynasty <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pharaoh">pharaoh</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khufu">Khufu</a> around 2560 BCE. Originally about 146 metres high, it remained the tallest man-made structure in the world for nearly four thousand years. Its construction shows the Old Kingdom's capacity to organise labour and resources, and it is the only surviving Wonder of the Ancient World.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/great-pyramid-of-giza.jpg" alt="Great Pyramid of Giza" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Douwe C. van der Zee · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Great_Pyramid_of_Giza_-_Pyramid_of_Khufu.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
